cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Value-Field Theory (VFT)"
message: "If you use this theory or repository, please cite this repository."
authors:
  - family-names: "Nuno"
    given-names: "T."
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
abstract: >
  Value-Field Theory (VFT) is a structural framework for describing how
  actor-relative, multidimensional real resource and capital states K and
  nominal or expectation structures P form a value field whose attraction is
  realized through actors' actions and decisions A. Each actor can access a
  different K and observe or reference a different P. P is treated as a
  history-dependent expectation stock, while E[Delta K] is represented
  separately as an expectation flow for a specified interval rather than as a
  required intermediate variable in action generation. For multi-actor actions,
  an intra-period equilibrium is the point at which the actors' expected Delta K
  are mutually consistent with the same transaction, contract, or joint action
  becoming feasible; this condition does not apply to actions completed by a
  single actor alone. Actions can change both K and P, while non-agentic changes
  to K such as depreciation or natural loss are treated only as an exception
  note. At aggregate scales, Delta P and Delta K can serve as principal proxies
  when full action tracking is too costly.
repository-code: "https://github.com/nuno929/vf-model"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
keywords:
  - value-field theory
  - multidimensional state
  - multi-actor system
